# Line endings are part of this repository's provenance. `results/usage.jsonl` is identified by the
# SHA-256 of its bytes, so a checkout that rewrites LF to CRLF silently changes the artifact every
# hash in FREEZE.md refers to. Git on Windows defaults to `core.autocrlf=true`, which does exactly
# that, so the behaviour is pinned here rather than left to each machine's config.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git decide what is text and leaves binaries alone; `eol=lf` forces LF on checkout
# for whatever it decides is text. This covers the .py, .md, .toml, .lock, .jsonl, .env template,
# .gitignore and .python-version files in this repo without naming them individually.
#
# `.secrets/typesafe.env` is local-only and ignored, so it is never checked out and no rule here
# concerns it.
* text=auto eol=lf
